        "type": "markdown-mermaid",
        "title": "How a closed basin develops a saline floor",
        "content": "```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  A[\"Surrounding catchment\"] -->|\"Runoff carries sediment and dissolved salts\"| B[\"Closed basin\"]\n  B -->|\"Sediment settles\"| C[\"Fine-grained basin floor\"]\n  B -->|\"Water evaporates\"| D[\"Dissolved salts concentrate\"]\n  C -->|\"Saline deposits accumulate\"| E[\"Playa or kavir surface\"]\n  D -->|\"Salt crystallizes\"| E\n```",
        "summary": "The arrows describe sediment delivery and salt concentration in a closed basin. This is a simplified landscape-forming process, not a diagnosis of desertification or an explanation of every salt deposit in Iran.",
